(r"""- **(e) ABSORBED, OR KEPT.** Once the levy is up and the army marches, the riders fold into the field force by default (§3.2): the roads behind go unpatrolled — the slow half fades, the counter term turns negative (§6.2), and brigandage rises in the rear and dens grow behind the lines (ST's dens and WC-12's bodies, by construction). A chooser that KEEPS its riders keeps its rear safe and fields a smaller army (`patrolDraw`, §6.6): ONE bounded chooser signal through THE CHOOSER'S SHARED-SIGNAL CAR (SX-08; the first chain to land owns the car; PR adds one term row, `keepRiders`, read from the court's risk posture — `strategicPosture.js`, requirement 10 — and the believed rear danger).""",
r"""- **(e) THE ARMY'S ROAD, THE REAR, AND WHAT IS KEPT.** When the levy is up and the army marches, the court keeps `CAMPAIGN_SHARE` of its envelope by default and those riders take the army's road out first (§3.2); the riders not kept fold into the field force, and the halves the kept riders cannot reach — the back roads, the rear — go unpatrolled: the slow half fades over four weeks, the counter term turns negative (§6.2), and brigandage rises in the rear and dens grow behind the lines (ST's dens and WC-12's bodies, by construction). A chooser that KEEPS MORE riders keeps its rear safe and marches a smaller army — the draw taken at that deploy (`patrolDraw`, §6.6): ONE bounded chooser signal through THE CHOOSER'S SHARED-SIGNAL CAR (SX-08; the first chain to land owns the car; PR adds one term row, `keepRiders`, read from the court's risk posture — `strategicPosture.js`, requirement 10 — and the believed rear danger), read when the army is raised and not again until it is raised anew [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-3 · PR-r2-1]."""),
