(r"""- **WHERE THE HOLD ALLOWS.** Only where the root's hold over the member reads `staunch` or `unbroken` (`polityHold`, PL §2; PL's own read `polityHoldOf(…)`); under `shaky` they keep to the root's own land and the stretches between members; under `frayed` they keep to the root's land and members ignore them.""",
r"""- **WHERE THE HOLD ALLOWS.** Only where the crown's OWN read of its hold is `staunch` or `unbroken` — `polityHoldOf(worldState, snapshot, rootId, rootId)`, the crown deciding on its own belief (PL §2's observer rule) — AND its reach into the member is live, `crownReachAt(worldState, snapshot, rootId, memberId, rootId).share01 > 0` (a direct vassal by `POLITY_LIEGE_SHARE`; a sub-vassal only as far as the reach carries — nothing under a frayed link); under `shaky` they keep to the root's own land and the roads between members; under `frayed` they keep to the root's land and members ignore them [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-20]."""),
(r"""- **THE CROWN'S SUMMONS — `patrol_order` (CLIMAX).** At war, the root may ORDER members' riders onto the war's roads (a small summons beside PL's service obligations): heard at the member's seat, verdicts `sent · kept` (PL's `relief_answer` words in the same sense: the member SENDS its riders or KEEPS them), the default the member's own fork — its deference (PL's seat-weight band), its own believed threat, its war exhaustion. `sent` moves the member's riders under the crown's round for the war's season and is credited like WC-1's contribution; `kept` is priced through PL's fealty door as a `service_refused` row (PL's `fealtyRecord`; PL owns the row, PR requests it — RULINGS-ROUND2 A.14's ONE-writer rule). [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final) — R-13: the brief's `answered · refused`; `answered` is a landed literal (5 files: a ransom reason, the razing's peace reason) and PL already holds the same act's words.]""",
r"""- **THE CROWN'S CALL ON THE RIDERS — PL's summons; no kind of PR's.** At war, the crown's call on a member's fighting men is PL-5's SUMMONS, answered on WC's `call_in_answer` (`answered · half_answered · refused · lapsed`; PL §4.1), and a member's riders are inside that levy (PR3) — so the riders ride the SAME card as ONE input line: `answered` — the member's riders go with its levy (those the crown's round can use ride the war's roads under `command: 'paramount'` for the war's season, credited like WC-1's contribution); `half_answered` — the member sends its levy and KEEPS its riders on its own roads (PL §4: "Half service — WC's `half_answered`; a `service_answered` row with the fraction"); `refused` — neither (PL prices it `service_refused` through its own writer, as for any refusal); `lapsed` — undecided. PR mints NO summons kind, no second vocabulary and no fealty row of its own, so no `requestFealtyRow` prefix is needed for riders [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-17 · SEAMS-r2-10: `patrol_order` double-heard the men PL's summons already hears, reversed `relief_answer`'s subject, and named the relationship writer's internal append instead of PL's request door; R-13 is withdrawn — the fold already uses `answered` for this act]."""),
(r"""- **A FORT'S GARRISON PATROLS** (ST): a held `fortification` puts its attached stretches first on the round (§2.2) and its holder's riders count from the fort's funded garrison (ST §4.1's holder rule: the town itself or a non-hostile settlement's garrison); a held `watchtower` extends the riders' NOTICE (§8.1's `tower`) and witnesses for them (ST17); DENS are what riders clear (ST's `site_cleared`, §5.3).""",
r"""- **A FORT'S GARRISON PATROLS** (ST §7.4's row): a held `fortification` puts its attached halves FIRST on its HOLDER's round (§2.2), and the riders who walk them are the holder town's OWN — drawn from its one envelope (§3), never a second count "from the fort's funded garrison"; the fort's garrison is ST's `siteDefense` on the walls (ST10). With `patrolsEnabled` lit, ST §3.3's fort ROAD terms — its presence suppression and its road watch gate rows ("A garrisoned keep watches the approaches.", "The keep's garrison keeps order on the roads.") — are ST's DARK ARM only: the lit fort watches its roads through its holder's riders plus ONE named lean, `fortWill` (a sound, funded keep at hand raises the holder's WILL gate one step, §3.1), so when the levy takes the riders the fort's road effect goes with them and "the hill road has gone to the brigands" holds beside a held fort too (ST's disposition aligns — a route row). Whether the fort's garrison is itself a stationed share of the holder's one head count (drawn as the riders are) is the chair's — ⛔ STOP SEAMS-r2-9 (§17) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — PR-r2-8: two manpower sources and a doubled road effect under one cap]. A held `watchtower` extends the riders' NOTICE (§8.1's `tower`) and witnesses for them (ST17); DENS are what riders clear (ST's `site_cleared`, §5.3). **SITES CONSIDERED** (RULINGS-ROUND2 E; ST §7.4's coverage row for PR, "BY BOTH"): the round reads the fort's attachment, the slow half shares ST's suppressor and cap, the clearing is ST's card, the tower is ST's witness — PR keeps no site number and mints no site record [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — the one "sites considered" line]."""),
